/godot/pull/104382#issuecomment-4952429804","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104382","id":4952429804,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJzAU7A","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-12T19:16:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-12T19:16:51Z","body":"> I compiled the engine with this PR locally and no. It removes the audio popping when an audio player goes in/out of the area but it adds a metallic sounding echo when the player is inside the area.\r\n> \r\n> Personally I don't use the built-in reverb zones exactly because of this - they are broken.\r\n\r\nRemoving the popping is the point of this PR, so in that case, I think it succeeded. As for the reverb, yea, that'd have to be addressed in a different PR. If you're talking about something different that clearly seems like a bug, I think you could record it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4952429804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"mini